{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"code","value":"function shouldThrowError<T>(throwOnError: boolean | T | undefined, params: Parameters<T>): boolean;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/utils.ts#L693","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/query-core/src/utils.ts:693"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Resolves a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"throwOnError"},{"type":"text","value":" option to a boolean.\nIf "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"throwOnError"},{"type":"text","value":" is a function, it is called with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"params"},{"type":"text","value":" (e.g. the error and, depending on the caller,\nadditional context such as the query or mutation) and its result is returned, allowing the throwing\nbehavior to be decided per error. Otherwise, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"throwOnError"},{"type":"text","value":" itself is coerced to a boolean ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"undefined"},{"type":"text","value":"\nresolves to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"false"},{"type":"text","value":")."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"type-parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"t","children":[{"type":"text","value":"T"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"T"},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"extends"}]},{"type":"text","value":" (..."},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"args"},{"type":"text","value":": "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"any"},{"type":"text","value":"[]) => "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"boolean"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"throwonerror","children":[{"type":"text","value":"throwOnError"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"boolean"},{"type":"text","value":" | "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"T"},{"type":"text","value":" | "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"undefined"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"throwOnError"},{"type":"text","value":" option: a boolean, a function that decides per error, or\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"undefined"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"params","children":[{"type":"text","value":"params"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Parameters"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"T"},{"type":"text","value":">"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The arguments passed to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"throwOnError"},{"type":"text","value":" if it is a function."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"boolean"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Whether the error should be thrown."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const throwOnError =\n  query.state.error && typeof options.throwOnError === 'function'\n    ? shouldThrowError(options.throwOnError, [query.state.error, query])\n    : options.throwOnError","lang":"ts"}],"headings":[{"id":"type-parameters","text":"Type Parameters","level":2},{"id":"t","text":"T","level":3},{"id":"parameters","text":"Parameters","level":2},{"id":"throwonerror","text":"throwOnError","level":3},{"id":"params","text":"params","level":3},{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":2},{"id":"example","text":"Example","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\nfunction shouldThrowError<T>(throwOnError: boolean | T | undefined, params: Parameters<T>): boolean;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/query-core/src/utils.ts:693](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/utils.ts#L693)\n\nResolves a `throwOnError` option to a boolean.\nIf `throwOnError` is a function, it is called with `params` (e.g. the error and, depending on the caller,\nadditional context such as the query or mutation) and its result is returned, allowing the throwing\nbehavior to be decided per error. Otherwise, `throwOnError` itself is coerced to a boolean (`undefined`\nresolves to `false`).\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### T\n\n`T` *extends* (...`args`: `any`[]) => `boolean`\n\n## Parameters\n\n### throwOnError\n\n`boolean` \\| `T` \\| `undefined`\n\nThe `throwOnError` option: a boolean, a function that decides per error, or\n`undefined`.\n\n### params\n\n`Parameters`\\<`T`\\>\n\nThe arguments passed to `throwOnError` if it is a function.\n\n## Returns\n\n`boolean`\n\nWhether the error should be thrown.\n\n## Example\n\n```ts\nconst throwOnError =\n  query.state.error && typeof options.throwOnError === 'function'\n    ? shouldThrowError(options.throwOnError, [query.state.error, query])\n    : options.throwOnError\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: shouldThrowError\ntitle: shouldThrowError\n---\n\n```ts\nfunction shouldThrowError<T>(throwOnError: boolean | T | undefined, params: Parameters<T>): boolean;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/query-core/src/utils.ts:693](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/utils.ts#L693)\n\nResolves a `throwOnError` option to a boolean.\nIf `throwOnError` is a function, it is called with `params` (e.g. the error and, depending on the caller,\nadditional context such as the query or mutation) and its result is returned, allowing the throwing\nbehavior to be decided per error. Otherwise, `throwOnError` itself is coerced to a boolean (`undefined`\nresolves to `false`).\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### T\n\n`T` *extends* (...`args`: `any`[]) => `boolean`\n\n## Parameters\n\n### throwOnError\n\n`boolean` \\| `T` \\| `undefined`\n\nThe `throwOnError` option: a boolean, a function that decides per error, or\n`undefined`.\n\n### params\n\n`Parameters`\\<`T`\\>\n\nThe arguments passed to `throwOnError` if it is a function.\n\n## Returns\n\n`boolean`\n\nWhether the error should be thrown.\n\n## Example\n\n```ts\nconst throwOnError =\n  query.state.error && typeof options.throwOnError === 'function'\n    ? shouldThrowError(options.throwOnError, [query.state.error, query])\n    : options.throwOnError\n```\n"}
